  "question": {
    "text": "The radius of curvature of each surface of a convex lens having refractive index <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The lens is now immersed in a liquid of refractive index <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>. The ratio of power of lens in air to its power in the liquid will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The power of a lens is given by&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>f</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>Using Lens Maker&#39;s&nbsp;formula,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.8</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>&#8722;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>immersed&#160;</mtext></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.8</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.5</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>&#8722;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Hence, the ratio is,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.8</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.8</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.5</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.8</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.5</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.3</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
